.TH MERMAN-CLI-BATCH 1 2026-08-15 "Merman 0.11.0" "Merman CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
merman\-cli\-batch \- Render every Mermaid diagram in one Markdown document
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmerman\-cli batch\fR [\fB\-\-stdin\-file\-name\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-svg\-pipeline\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-css\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scale\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-fit\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-fit\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-max\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-max\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-max\-pixels\fR] [\fB\-\-raster\-unbounded\fR] [\fB\-\-pdf\-filter\-scale\fR] [\fB\-\-pdf\-max\-filter\-image\-pixels\fR] [\fB\-\-pdf\-filter\-images\-unbounded\fR] [\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-total\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-pixels\fR] [\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-total\-pixels\fR] [\fB\-\-embedded\-images\-unbounded\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-private\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-icon\-pack\fR] [\fB\-\-icon\-pack\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-suppress\-errors\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-clock\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-timezone\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-random\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-timing\fR] [\fB\-\-fixed\-today\fR] [\fB\-\-fixed\-unix\-millis\fR] [\fB\-\-fixed\-local\-offset\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-appearance\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-precedence\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-background\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-measurement\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-max\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-font\-max\-measurements\fR] [\fB\-\-math\-renderer\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-svg\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-hand\-drawn\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-operation\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIINPUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render every Mermaid diagram in one Markdown document
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIINPUT\fR]
Input Markdown file. Use `\-` for stdin
.SH "BATCH INPUT AND OUTPUT"
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\-file\-name\fR \fI<STDIN_FILE_NAME>\fR
Logical source file name for Markdown read from stdin
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI<OUTPUT_DIR>\fR
Tool\-owned directory for the rewritten document and generated artifacts
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<JOBS>\fR
Maximum number of Markdown charts rendered concurrently
.SH "BATCH OUTPUT"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format. Defaults to SVG
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
svg
.IP \(bu 2
png
.IP \(bu 2
jpg
.IP \(bu 2
pdf
.RE
.SH "MERMAN RENDERER CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-svg\-pipeline\fR \fI<SVG_PIPELINE>\fR
SVG consumer: parity (default), static for fixed markup, or resvg\-safe for resvg/usvg.

Readable only adds text fallbacks for consumers that ignore HTML labels and can show duplicate text in browsers. PNG/JPEG/PDF use static generation and resvg\-safe conversion.
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
parity: Default for browsers and Webviews; preserves Mermaid HTML labels and styles
.IP \(bu 2
static: Generates SVG for fixed markup, emitting only the container palette slots it uses
.IP \(bu 2
readable: Advanced text fallback for consumers that ignore HTML labels; browsers may show duplicates
.IP \(bu 2
resvg\-safe: Converts HTML labels and cleans SVG for resvg/usvg consumers
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-math\-renderer\fR \fI<MATH_RENDERER>\fR
Math renderer override. Unspecified uses the compiled default; `ratex` requires `math`
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
none
.IP \(bu 2
ratex
.RE
.SH "MERMAID CONFIGURATION"
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-css\-file\fR \fI<CSS_FILE>\fR
CSS file injected into SVG output before export
.TP
\fB\-\-suppress\-errors\fR
Emit an error diagram instead of failing on parse errors
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\-file\fR \fI<CONFIG_FILE>\fR
JSON Mermaid configuration file
.SH "RENDER INPUT AND OUTPUT"
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-error log output
.SH "RASTER OUTPUT"
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-scale\fR \fI<SCALE>\fR
Raster output scale factor. Defaults to 1
.SH "MERMAN RASTER CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-fit\-width\fR \fI<RASTER_FIT_WIDTH>\fR
Fit raster output to this CSS\-pixel width before applying \-\-scale
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-fit\-height\fR \fI<RASTER_FIT_HEIGHT>\fR
Fit raster output to this CSS\-pixel height before applying \-\-scale
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-max\-width\fR \fI<RASTER_MAX_WIDTH>\fR
Maximum raster output width after scale and fit. Defaults to 4096
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-max\-height\fR \fI<RASTER_MAX_HEIGHT>\fR
Maximum raster output height after scale and fit. Defaults to 4096
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-max\-pixels\fR \fI<RASTER_MAX_PIXELS>\fR
Maximum raster output pixels after scale and fit. Defaults to 4096*4096
.TP
\fB\-\-raster\-unbounded\fR
Disable raster size limits. Use only for trusted oversized exports
.SH "MERMAN PDF CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-filter\-scale\fR \fI<FILTER_SCALE>\fR
Sampling scale for SVG filters that require localized PDF bitmaps. Defaults to 4
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-max\-filter\-image\-pixels\fR \fI<MAX_FILTER_IMAGE_PIXELS>\fR
Maximum aggregate pixels retained as localized PDF filter images. Defaults to 33554432
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-filter\-images\-unbounded\fR
Disable the retained PDF filter\-image pixel budget for trusted inputs
.SH "MERMAN EMBEDDED-IMAGE CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_IMAGE_BYTES>\fR
Maximum decoded data\-URL bytes for one embedded image. Defaults to 16777216
.TP
\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-total\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_TOTAL_BYTES>\fR
Maximum aggregate decoded data\-URL bytes for embedded images. Defaults to 33554432
.TP
\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-pixels\fR \fI<MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS>\fR
Maximum intrinsic pixels for one embedded raster image. Defaults to 16777216
.TP
\fB\-\-embedded\-image\-max\-total\-pixels\fR \fI<MAX_TOTAL_PIXELS>\fR
Maximum aggregate intrinsic pixels for embedded raster images. Defaults to 33554432
.TP
\fB\-\-embedded\-images\-unbounded\fR
Disable embedded raster image decode budgets for trusted inputs
.SH "ICON PACKS"
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-network\fR
Allow icon pack loading from public HTTP(S) destinations
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-private\-network\fR
Allow explicitly configured icon URLs to resolve to private or loopback addresses
.TP
\fB\-\-icon\-pack\fR \fI<PACKAGE_OR_PATH>\fR
Iconify package name or local package path. Can be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-icon\-pack\-source\fR \fI<PREFIX#SOURCE>\fR
Iconify prefix and source as PREFIX#SOURCE. Can be repeated
.SH "RUNTIME POLICY"
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR [default: deterministic]
Runtime source for clock, local timezone, and operation randomness
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
deterministic
.IP \(bu 2
native
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-clock\fR
Use the system clock while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-timezone\fR
Use the system local timezone while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-random\fR
Use system randomness while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-timing\fR
Enable operation timing diagnostics through the compiled system timing adapter
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed\-today\fR \fI<FIXED_TODAY>\fR
Override the local "today" date for time\-dependent diagrams
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed\-unix\-millis\fR \fI<FIXED_UNIX_MILLIS>\fR
Override the clock with exact Unix milliseconds within the JavaScript Date range.
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed\-local\-offset\-minutes\fR \fI<FIXED_LOCAL_OFFSET_MINUTES>\fR
Override the local timezone offset in minutes for time\-dependent diagrams
.SH THEME
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<ID_OR_PATH>\fR
Merman preset ID, v2 JSON file (`\-` for stdin), or Mermaid theme ID
.TP
\fB\-\-appearance\fR \fI<APPEARANCE>\fR
Appearance for a native preset or document. Defaults to the selected theme\*(Aqs default
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-precedence\fR \fI<THEME_PRECEDENCE>\fR [default: host]
Decide whether the CLI selection or a source\-authored Mermaid theme takes precedence
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
host
.IP \(bu 2
source
.RE
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-background\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Override the diagram canvas with a color or `transparent`
.SH "NATIVE FONTS"
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Load a local font file and enable native Mermaid text measurement; repeatable, earlier sources take precedence
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Load fonts from a bounded directory scan and enable native Mermaid text measurement; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-measurement\fR \fI<FONT_MEASUREMENT>\fR
Text measurement: SVG defaults to deterministic; PNG/JPEG/PDF use native fonts for shared layout and painting. Explicit deterministic keeps approximate layout
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
deterministic
.IP \(bu 2
native
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-system\fR \fI<FONT_SYSTEM>\fR
Control system font discovery. Native encoded output enables it by default. The values on, bounded, and platform enable system fallback for explicit fonts.
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
on: Enable the build\*(Aqs default system font provider
.IP \(bu 2
bounded: Use Merman\*(Aqs bounded system font discovery
.IP \(bu 2
platform: Query the platform\*(Aqs font catalog. Platform metadata access is outside Merman\*(Aqs scan limits
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-max\-bytes\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Byte budget for the entire native font context, including explicit and selected system fonts (default 256 MiB). Use a positive integer in bytes or with a KiB, MiB, or GiB suffix, such as 256MiB
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-max\-measurements\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Maximum uncached native font shaping probes per diagram (default: 16384); independent of \-\-resource\-profile
.SH "LAYOUT VIEWPORT"
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fI<CONTAINER_WIDTH>\fR
Available container width for size\-sensitive layouts
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-height\fR \fI<CONTAINER_HEIGHT>\fR
Available container height for size\-sensitive layouts
.SH "SVG OUTPUT"
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-svg\-id\fR \fI<SVG_ID>\fR
Root SVG id and internal marker prefix
.SH "DETERMINISTIC RENDERING"
.TP
\fB\-\-hand\-drawn\-seed\fR \fI<HAND_DRAWN_SEED>\fR
Stabilize rough/hand\-drawn rendering where supported
.SH "RESOURCE CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR [default: trusted\-native]
Resource policy for input, semantic models, output, and CLI acquisition.

Use interactive for cooperative editor\-like workloads, constrained for untrusted or multi\-tenant input, and trusted\-native for controlled local workloads. Unbounded\-for\-trusted\-input removes all policy budgets, retaining hard implementation and protocol guards. Use \-\-resource\-limit for a scoped increase.
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
interactive: General interactive applications and public binding surfaces
.IP \(bu 2
constrained: Constrained rendering for untrusted or publicly submitted documents
.IP \(bu 2
trusted\-native: Local CLI and controlled native batch rendering
.IP \(bu 2
unbounded\-for\-trusted\-input: Explicitly disable policy budgets while retaining hard backend capabilities
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR \fI<STABLE_ID=POSITIVE_U64>\fR
Override a resource budget as STABLE_ID=POSITIVE_U64. Can be repeated
.SH "OPERATION CONTROL"
.TP
\fB\-\-operation\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MILLISECONDS>\fR
Cancel the complete command operation after this many milliseconds.

The deadline starts before input acquisition and covers generation, rendering, and publication. Omit this option for no deadline. Zero cancels at the first cooperative checkpoint. Resource budgets are independent; an unbounded resource profile does not disable this deadline. Blocking backend calls return to a checkpoint before cancellation.
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  merman\-cli batch README.md

More options: `merman\-cli batch \-\-help` shows advanced renderer, resource, and security controls.
.SH VERSION
v0.11.0
